<title>USA: High pressure dominates Brazil coffee belt - WSC.</title>
<headline>High pressure dominates Brazil coffee belt - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Warm, high pressure aloft over Brazil is expected to dominate the coffee belt for the coming week, Weather Services Corp said in an update on Friday.</p>
<p>Fair skies were observed in main growing areas of the belt this morning. Low temperatures were in the 50's F (10-15 C). Some cooler conditions were reported in higher elevations.</p>
<p>Mosstly fair skies are expected for the next seven days. Temperatures should be near normal levels for this time of year. Low temperatures will be in the 50's to low 60's F (low to middle teens C). Cooler conditions are still expected for higher elevations, although there is still no damaging cold indicated, according to WSC. ((--Eileen Houlihan, New York Commodity Desk, 212-859-1640))</p>
